"lib/db.kfx: the query database, salsa's design, in KFX (kc's K0,
 `docs/research/kc.md`; `docs/research/compilation-service.md`; Coopt's
 `coopt-query`, whose design it follows, read at 9283bba). A query is a
 function of a key whose body reads inputs and other queries only through
 the database; the database records what each read, in the order read,
 and on a later ask re-runs a query only if something it read has changed
 since it was last made sure of:

 - **Revisions**: setting an input to a new value moves the database to a
   new revision. A node says the revision it was last verified in, and
   the one its value last changed in.
 - **Durability**: an input is set at a durability, 0 (a draft) to 3
   (fixed); a node keeps the least of what it read. A node whose least
   durability no input changed at since it was verified is current at
   once (`last`: for each durability, the revision an input of that
   durability or more last changed in).
 - **Verification** walks a node's reads in order, each made current
   first; the first that changed after the node was verified sends it to
   be run again (rustc's rule: after one changed, the body might have read
   other things). A node verified so takes its reads' least durability as
   it is now (C400).
 - **Modelled** in `models/db.qnt` (Quint), checked by its simulator.
 - **Early cutoff**: a node run again whose value has the fingerprint it
   had keeps its revision of change, so what read it stays current.
 - **Persisted** (C472, `kayak-db 3`): a head; the graph in shards, one
   for each group of keys (a program's file, most), each read when one of
   its keys is asked for, and written when one of its nodes changed; and
   each value kept in a file of its own, read when it is asked for. So a
   run reads and writes what it uses and changes, not the database whole
   (C417's two files, read and written whole, before: a run beside the
   expander's 43 MB took 0.94 s, not 0.012 s). `db-saved`, `db-opened`.

 Keys are data (C417; the user: \"Making keys structured data is totally
 up my alley\"): a query's name and its arguments, `(l0-item \"PATH\"
 \"KEY\")`, each interned as a number the first time it is met, by its
 text, so that the nodes are found by number and what a node read is a
 list of numbers. Values are text, the database's alone: a query's value is
 what its body gives as text, its fingerprint FNV-1a of it
 (`lib/query.kfx`). The bodies are one procedure the client gives every
 ask, `run`, which is given a key and runs that key's query: so the
 database's type names no procedure of itself.

 Synchronous, as K0 is: a body runs to its end, its asks nested in it. In
 one region, `@q`, and of one effect, `qe`, every body's (the compiler's
 passes are pure); over effects and regions when a client needs it.
 A cycle of asks is refused, as an error."

"`nondet` (C415): a body may `attempt` a pass, so that a refusal is its
 value and not the end of the run; what a failure says is the machine's,
 which a database of one compiler's (its identity in its first line) has
 one of."
"And a body may build and run a program (C449): a procedural macro's
 transformer's answer, `phase1 REQUEST`, a query whose body checks,
 compiles, builds and runs the transformer, as deterministic as any of
 its key, the request's text, its files named by what they hold. Since
 C454 it runs it in process: its image sealed in the code area and
 called, through its runtime's syscalls."
(define-effect qe (maxeff (read @globals) spin nondet (read @q) (write @q) (alloc @q)
                          (io process) (io fs-read) (io fs-write) (io stderr) (io exit) (alloc @io) (read @io) (write @io)
                          ;; A body that runs native code in process (C454: kc's
                          ;; transformers, sealed in the code area and called,
                          ;; their runtime's syscalls).
                          (io native) (io sys)))

"A value as a node keeps it (C472): its text, made in this run and not
 yet in a file; its text, as its file has it (read, or written); in its
 file, not read yet (the node's number, which names the file); in its
 shard's file, a small one (C473): the shard's number, its offset in the
 shard's values and length, and whether it is escaped there (past ASCII),
 cut out when it is read; or none, a value the database was not asked to
 keep, made again when it is read."
(define-datatype value (v-text string) (v-read string) (v-file i64) (v-at i64 i64 i64 bool) (v-none))

"A node: its key; whether it is an input; the revision it was verified
 in; the one its value changed in; its value's fingerprint; what it read,
 in order, by number; the least durability of that (an input's, its own);
 its value."
(define-datatype node (node sexp bool i64 i64 i64 (listof i64 acyclic) i64 value))

"Nodes by number, and numbers by a key's text: AVL trees, as
 `lib/query.kfx`'s `fmap`."
(define-datatype imap (im-none) (im-node imap i64 node i64 imap))
(define-datatype kmap (km-none) (km-node kmap string i64 i64 kmap))

"A query being run: its key's number, what it has read so far (the newest
 first), and the least durability of that."
(define-datatype frame (frame i64 (listof i64 acyclic) i64))

"A shard of the graph (C472): the keys of one group, a key's first
 argument (a file's path, most) or its query's name, and their nodes. Its
 group's hash, by which the head names it; the slot its file is in (0 or
 1; -1, none yet); its file's text, once read (its nodes' records read
 from it as they are asked for); the next number within it; whether it is
 read, and whether a node of it changed since."
(define-datatype shard (shard string i64 string i64 bool bool))
(define-datatype smap (sm-none) (sm-node smap i64 shard i64 smap))

"What reads a file of the database by its name (`` the head's): its text,
 or `` if there is none."
(define-type reader (subr qe (string) string))

"The database: the revision; the nodes, by number, those read or made; the
 numbers, by key, of the shards read; the shards, by number, and their
 numbers by their groups' hashes; how many; what reads its files; the
 queries being run, the innermost first; for each durability, 0 to 3, the
 revision an input of it or more last changed in; how many times a body
 has run, and whose (for tests and measures)."
(define-type db
  (productof (rev (ref i64 @q))
             (nodes (ref imap @q))
             (ids (ref kmap @q))
             (shards (ref smap @q))
             (groups (ref kmap @q))
             (nshards (ref i64 @q))
             (reads (ref reader @q))
             (dirty (ref bool @q))
             (frames (ref (listof frame acyclic) @q))
             (last (ref (listof i64 acyclic) @q))
             (runs (ref i64 @q))
             (ran (ref sexps @q))))

"What runs a query: given the database and a key, its value."
(define-type runner (subr qe (db sexp) string))

(define durabilities i64 4)

"A node's number (C472): its shard's number times `shard-span`, and its
 place within the shard; so that a number a node read names its shard."
(define shard-span i64 16777216)
(define shard-of-number (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (i) (i64-quotient i shard-span)))

;;; ------------------------------------------------------------ keys

"A key of a query of one argument, or two: `(NAME \"A\")`, `(NAME \"A\" \"B\")`."
(define key1 (subr kfx (string string) sexp)
  (lambda (q a) (lst (list (sym q "" 0) (str a "" 0)) "" 0 0)))

(define key2 (subr kfx (string string string) sexp)
  (lambda (q a b) (lst (list (sym q "" 0) (str a "" 0) (str b "" 0)) "" 0 0)))

"A key's query's name, and its argument `i` (from 0) as text."
(define key-query (subr kfx (sexp) string)
  (lambda (k) (tagcase k (lst (xs f l p) (if (null? xs) "" (tagcase (car xs) (sym (n f2 p2) n) (else other "")))) (sym (n f p) n) (else other ""))))

(define-rec
  (key-arg (subr kfx (sexp i64) string)
    (lambda (k i)
      (tagcase k
        (lst (xs f l p) (key-arg-of (cdr xs) i))
        (else other ""))))
  (key-arg-of (subr kfx (sexps i64) string)
    (lambda (xs i)
      (cond ((null? xs) "")
            ((i64= i 0) (tagcase (car xs) (str (s f p) s) (sym (s f p) s) (num (n f p) (i64->string n)) (else other "")))
            (else (key-arg-of (cdr xs) (i64- i 1)))))))

(define-rec
  (hex-of (subr kfx (i64 string) string)
    (lambda (n acc)
      (let* ((d (i64-remainder n 16))
             (acc (string-append (list->string (list (i64->char (if (i64< d 10) (i64+ d 48) (i64+ d 87))))) acc)))
        (if (i64< n 16) acc (hex-of (i64-quotient n 16) acc))))))

"A key as text, the one text of every key alike: how it is interned, and
 how it is written."
(define-rec
  (key-escaped (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) (listof string acyclic)) (listof string acyclic))
    (lambda (cs acc)
      (if (null? cs)
          acc
          (key-escaped (cdr cs)
                       (cons (cond ((char=? (car cs) #\") "\\\"")
                                   ((char=? (car cs) #\\) "\\\\")
                                   ((char=? (car cs) #\newline) "\\n")
                                   ((char=? (car cs) #\tab) "\\t")
                                   ;; Past ASCII, so that the graph is ASCII (C417).
                                   ((i64> (char->i64 (car cs)) 127) (string-append "\\u{" (string-append (hex-of (char->i64 (car cs)) "") "}")))
                                   (else (list->string (list (car cs)))))
                             acc))))))

(define-rec
  (plain-from? (subr kfx (string i64 i64) bool)
    (lambda (s i n)
      "Whether `s` from `i` needs no escape: no `\"`, `\\`, control or past-ASCII
       character. By index, a string's characters not made a list."
      (if (i64>= i n)
          #t
          (let ((k (char->i64 (string-ref-i64 s i))))
            (and (i64>= k 32) (i64<= k 126) (not (i64= k 34)) (not (i64= k 92)) (plain-from? s (i64+ i 1) n)))))))

(define str-text (subr kfx (string) string)
  (lambda (s)
    (if (plain-from? s 0 (string-length-i64 s))
        (string-append "\"" (string-append s "\""))
        (string-append "\"" (string-append (string-list-append (reverse (key-escaped (string-chars s) nil))) "\"")))))

(define-rec
  (key-text (subr kfx (sexp) string)
    (lambda (k)
      (tagcase k
        (sym (n f p) n)
        (str (s f p) (str-text s))
        (num (n f p) (i64->string n))
        (lst (xs f l p) (string-append "(" (string-append (keys-text xs) ")")))
        (else other "?"))))
  (keys-text (subr kfx (sexps) string)
    (lambda (xs)
      (cond ((null? xs) "")
            ((null? (cdr xs)) (key-text (car xs)))
            (else (string-append (key-text (car xs)) (string-append " " (keys-text (cdr xs)))))))))

;;; ------------------------------------------------------------ the trees

(define im-height (subr kfx (imap) i64)
  (lambda (t) (tagcase t (im-none () 0) (im-node (l k x h r) h))))

(define im-make (subr kfx (imap i64 node imap) imap)
  (lambda (l k x r) (im-node l k x (i64+ 1 (let ((a (im-height l)) (b (im-height r))) (if (i64> a b) a b))) r)))

(define im-balanced (subr kfx (imap i64 node imap) imap)
  (lambda (l k x r)
    (let ((hl (im-height l)) (hr (im-height r)))
      (cond ((i64> hl (i64+ hr 1))
             (tagcase l
               (im-node (ll lk lx lh lr)
                 (if (i64>= (im-height ll) (im-height lr))
                     (im-make ll lk lx (im-make lr k x r))
                     (tagcase lr (im-node (rl rk rx rh rr) (im-make (im-make ll lk lx rl) rk rx (im-make rr k x r))) (im-none () (im-make l k x r)))))
               (im-none () (im-make l k x r))))
            ((i64> hr (i64+ hl 1))
             (tagcase r
               (im-node (rl rk rx rh rr)
                 (if (i64>= (im-height rr) (im-height rl))
                     (im-make (im-make l k x rl) rk rx rr)
                     (tagcase rl (im-node (ml mk mx mh mr) (im-make (im-make l k x ml) mk mx (im-make mr rk rx rr))) (im-none () (im-make l k x r)))))
               (im-none () (im-make l k x r))))
            (else (im-make l k x r))))))

(define-rec
  (im-put (subr kfx (imap i64 node) imap)
    (lambda (t n x)
      (tagcase t
        (im-none () (im-node (im-none) n x 1 (im-none)))
        (im-node (l k y h r)
          (cond ((i64= n k) (im-node l k x h r))
                ((i64< n k) (im-balanced (im-put l n x) k y r))
                (else (im-balanced l k y (im-put r n x))))))))
  (im-get (subr kfx (imap i64) (listof node acyclic))
    (lambda (t n)
      "`n`'s node, as a list of one, or none."
      (tagcase t
        (im-none () nil)
        (im-node (l k x h r) (cond ((i64= n k) (list x)) ((i64< n k) (im-get l n)) (else (im-get r n))))))))

(define-rec
  (im-list (subr kfx (imap (listof i64 acyclic)) (listof i64 acyclic))
    (lambda (t acc)
      "The numbers, in order, onto `acc`."
      (tagcase t
        (im-none () acc)
        (im-node (l k x h r) (im-list l (cons k (im-list r acc))))))))

(define km-height (subr kfx (kmap) i64)
  (lambda (t) (tagcase t (km-none () 0) (km-node (l k x h r) h))))

(define km-make (subr kfx (kmap string i64 kmap) kmap)
  (lambda (l k x r) (km-node l k x (i64+ 1 (let ((a (km-height l)) (b (km-height r))) (if (i64> a b) a b))) r)))

(define km-balanced (subr kfx (kmap string i64 kmap) kmap)
  (lambda (l k x r)
    (let ((hl (km-height l)) (hr (km-height r)))
      (cond ((i64> hl (i64+ hr 1))
             (tagcase l
               (km-node (ll lk lx lh lr)
                 (if (i64>= (km-height ll) (km-height lr))
                     (km-make ll lk lx (km-make lr k x r))
                     (tagcase lr (km-node (rl rk rx rh rr) (km-make (km-make ll lk lx rl) rk rx (km-make rr k x r))) (km-none () (km-make l k x r)))))
               (km-none () (km-make l k x r))))
            ((i64> hr (i64+ hl 1))
             (tagcase r
               (km-node (rl rk rx rh rr)
                 (if (i64>= (km-height rr) (km-height rl))
                     (km-make (km-make l k x rl) rk rx rr)
                     (tagcase rl (km-node (ml mk mx mh mr) (km-make (km-make l k x ml) mk mx (km-make mr rk rx rr))) (km-none () (km-make l k x r)))))
               (km-none () (km-make l k x r))))
            (else (km-make l k x r))))))

(define-rec
  (km-put (subr kfx (kmap string i64) kmap)
    (lambda (t n x)
      (tagcase t
        (km-none () (km-node (km-none) n x 1 (km-none)))
        (km-node (l k y h r)
          (cond ((string=? n k) (km-node l k x h r))
                ((string<? n k) (km-balanced (km-put l n x) k y r))
                (else (km-balanced l k y (km-put r n x))))))))
  (km-get (subr kfx (kmap string) i64)
    (lambda (t n)
      "`n`'s number; -1 if it has none."
      (tagcase t
        (km-none () -1)
        (km-node (l k x h r) (cond ((string=? n k) x) ((string<? n k) (km-get l n)) (else (km-get r n))))))))

;;; ------------------------------------------------------------ the fields

(define node-key (subr kfx (node) sexp) (lambda (n) (tagcase n (node (k i v c f ds du x) k))))
(define node-input? (subr kfx (node) bool) (lambda (n) (tagcase n (node (k i v c f ds du x) i))))
(define node-verified (subr kfx (node) i64) (lambda (n) (tagcase n (node (k i v c f ds du x) v))))
(define node-changed (subr kfx (node) i64) (lambda (n) (tagcase n (node (k i v c f ds du x) c))))
(define node-fp (subr kfx (node) i64) (lambda (n) (tagcase n (node (k i v c f ds du x) f))))
(define node-deps (subr kfx (node) (listof i64 acyclic)) (lambda (n) (tagcase n (node (k i v c f ds du x) ds))))
(define node-durability (subr kfx (node) i64) (lambda (n) (tagcase n (node (k i v c f ds du x) du))))
(define node-kept (subr kfx (node) value) (lambda (n) (tagcase n (node (k i v c f ds du x) x))))

(define node-verified-at (subr kfx (node i64) node)
  (lambda (n r) (tagcase n (node (k i v c f ds du x) (node k i r c f ds du x)))))

(define node-reverified (subr kfx (node i64 i64) node)
  (lambda (n r d) (tagcase n (node (k i v c f ds du x) (node k i r c f ds d x)))))

(define node-has-value? (subr kfx (node) bool)
  (lambda (n) (tagcase (node-kept n) (v-none () #f) (else other #t))))

(define-rec
  (db-nth (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic) i64) i64)
    (lambda (xs i) (cond ((null? xs) 0) ((i64= i 0) (car xs)) (else (db-nth (cdr xs) (i64- i 1)))))))

(define-rec
  (bumped (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic) i64 i64 i64) (listof i64 acyclic))
    (lambda (xs d r i)
      "`xs`, each of durability `i` up to `d` made `r`."
      (if (null? xs) nil (cons (if (i64<= i d) r (car xs)) (bumped (cdr xs) d r (i64+ i 1)))))))

(define-rec
  (zeros (subr kfx (i64) (listof i64 acyclic))
    (lambda (n) (if (i64<= n 0) nil (cons 0 (zeros (i64- n 1)))))))

(define-rec
  (id-in? (subr kfx (i64 (listof frame acyclic)) bool)
    (lambda (k fs)
      (cond ((null? fs) #f)
            ((tagcase (car fs) (frame (fk ds du) (i64= fk k))) #t)
            (else (id-in? k (cdr fs)))))))

"The graph's scanner's first parts (C417)."
(define-datatype scanned (scanned i64 i64))
(define sc-char (subr kfx (string i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (s i n) (if (i64< i n) (char->i64 (string-ref-i64 s i)) -1)))

(define-rec
  (sc-ws (subr kfx (string i64 i64) i64)
    (lambda (s i n) (let ((c (sc-char s i n))) (if (or (i64= c 32) (i64= c 10)) (sc-ws s (i64+ i 1) n) i)))))

(define-rec
  (sc-close (subr kfx (string i64 i64) i64)
    (lambda (s i n) (let ((c (sc-char s i n))) (if (or (i64< c 0) (i64= c 41)) i (sc-close s (i64+ i 1) n))))))

(define-rec
  (sc-digits (subr kfx (string i64 i64 i64) scanned)
    (lambda (s i n acc)
      (let ((c (sc-char s i n)))
        (if (and (i64>= c 48) (i64<= c 57)) (sc-digits s (i64+ i 1) n (i64+ (i64* acc 10) (i64- c 48))) (scanned acc i))))))

"The number at `i`, after any spaces; and where it ends."
(define sc-int (subr kfx (string i64 i64) scanned)
  (lambda (s i n)
    (let ((i (sc-ws s i n)))
      (if (i64= (sc-char s i n) 45)
          (tagcase (sc-digits s (i64+ i 1) n 0) (scanned (v e) (scanned (i64- 0 v) e)))
          (sc-digits s i n 0)))))

(define-rec
  (labels-scanned (subr kfx (string i64 i64 (listof i64 acyclic)) (listof i64 acyclic))
    (lambda (s i n acc)
      "The `#N#`s of a node's reads, to their `)`, in order."
      (let ((i (sc-ws s i n)))
        (if (not (i64= (sc-char s i n) 35))
            (reverse acc)
            (tagcase (sc-digits s (i64+ i 1) n 0)
              (scanned (k e) (labels-scanned s (i64+ e 1) n (cons k acc)))))))))

(define-rec
  (sc-ints (subr kfx (string i64 i64 i64 (listof i64 acyclic)) (listof i64 acyclic))
    (lambda (s i n count acc)
      (if (i64<= count 0)
          (reverse (cons i acc))
          (tagcase (sc-int s i n) (scanned (v e) (sc-ints s e n (i64- count 1) (cons v acc))))))))

"A node's record of the graph at offset `i` (C417): `(LEN #N# INPUT
 VERIFIED CHANGED FINGERPRINT DURABILITY (#M# ...) VALUE)`, its key `key`."
(define node-record (subr kfx (string i64 sexp) node)
  (lambda (s i key)
    (let ((n (string-length-i64 s)))
      (tagcase (sc-int s (i64+ i 1) n)
        (scanned (len b)
          (tagcase (sc-digits s (i64+ b 2) n 0)
            (scanned (k e)
              (let* ((ns (sc-ints s (i64+ e 1) n 5 nil))
                     (p (sc-ws s (db-nth ns 5) n))
                     (deps (labels-scanned s (i64+ p 1) n nil))
                     (v (sc-ws s (i64+ (sc-close s (i64+ p 1) n) 1) n))
                     ;; `file` (C472): its value in the file its number names;
                     ;; `(at O L)`, `(atx O L)` (C473), in the shard's values.
                     (val (cond ((i64= (sc-char s v n) 102) (v-file k))
                                ((i64= (sc-char s v n) 40)
                                 (let* ((x (i64= (sc-char s (i64+ v 3) n) 120))
                                        (os (sc-ints s (i64+ v (if x 4 3)) n 2 nil)))
                                   (v-at (shard-of-number k) (db-nth os 0) (db-nth os 1) x)))
                                (else (v-none)))))
                (node key (i64= (db-nth ns 0) 1) (db-nth ns 1) (db-nth ns 2) (db-nth ns 3) deps (db-nth ns 4) val)))))))))

"Reading them back: the graph scanned by offset (C417), never made a list
 of its characters, nor a datum: it is ASCII alone, so an offset is a
 character's. A key's text, by which it is interned, is made of its parts as
 written, which the writer wrote as `key-text` writes them."
(define-datatype atom (atom sexp string))
(define-datatype amap (am-none) (am-node amap i64 atom i64 amap))
(define-datatype part (part sexp string amap i64))
(define-datatype parts (parts sexps (listof string acyclic) amap i64))

(define am-height (subr kfx (amap) i64) (lambda (t) (tagcase t (am-none () 0) (am-node (l k x h r) h))))
(define am-make (subr kfx (amap i64 atom amap) amap)
  (lambda (l k x r) (am-node l k x (i64+ 1 (let ((a (am-height l)) (b (am-height r))) (if (i64> a b) a b))) r)))
(define am-balanced (subr kfx (amap i64 atom amap) amap)
  (lambda (l k x r)
    (let ((hl (am-height l)) (hr (am-height r)))
      (cond ((i64> hl (i64+ hr 1))
             (tagcase l
               (am-node (ll lk lx lh lr)
                 (if (i64>= (am-height ll) (am-height lr))
                     (am-make ll lk lx (am-make lr k x r))
                     (tagcase lr (am-node (rl rk rx rh rr) (am-make (am-make ll lk lx rl) rk rx (am-make rr k x r))) (am-none () (am-make l k x r)))))
               (am-none () (am-make l k x r))))
            ((i64> hr (i64+ hl 1))
             (tagcase r
               (am-node (rl rk rx rh rr)
                 (if (i64>= (am-height rr) (am-height rl))
                     (am-make (am-make l k x rl) rk rx rr)
                     (tagcase rl (am-node (ml mk mx mh mr) (am-make (am-make l k x ml) mk mx (am-make mr rk rx rr))) (am-none () (am-make l k x r)))))
               (am-none () (am-make l k x r))))
            (else (am-make l k x r))))))
(define-rec
  (am-put (subr kfx (amap i64 atom) amap)
    (lambda (t n x)
      (tagcase t
        (am-none () (am-node (am-none) n x 1 (am-none)))
        (am-node (l k y h r)
          (cond ((i64= n k) (am-node l k x h r))
                ((i64< n k) (am-balanced (am-put l n x) k y r))
                (else (am-balanced l k y (am-put r n x))))))))
  (am-get (subr kfx (amap i64) (listof atom acyclic))
    (lambda (t n)
      (tagcase t
        (am-none () nil)
        (am-node (l k x h r) (cond ((i64= n k) (list x)) ((i64< n k) (am-get l n)) (else (am-get r n))))))))

(define-rec
  (sc-str-end (subr kfx (string i64 i64 i64) scanned)
    (lambda (s i n esc)
      "From inside a string's quotes: whether a `\\` is in it (1), and where
       its closing quote is."
      (let ((c (sc-char s i n)))
        (cond ((i64< c 0) (scanned esc i))
              ((i64= c 92) (sc-str-end s (i64+ i 2) n 1))
              ((i64= c 34) (scanned esc i))
              (else (sc-str-end s (i64+ i 1) n esc)))))))

(define-rec
  (str-unescaped (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) (listof char acyclic)) string)
    (lambda (cs acc)
      (cond ((null? cs) (list->string (reverse acc)))
            ((and (char=? (car cs) #\\) (not (null? (cdr cs))))
             (let ((e (car (cdr cs))))
               (cond ((char=? e #\n) (str-unescaped (cdr (cdr cs)) (cons #\newline acc)))
                     ((char=? e #\t) (str-unescaped (cdr (cdr cs)) (cons #\tab acc)))
                     ((char=? e #\u) (str-code (cdr (cdr (cdr cs))) 0 acc))
                     (else (str-unescaped (cdr (cdr cs)) (cons e acc))))))
            (else (str-unescaped (cdr cs) (cons (car cs) acc))))))
  (str-code (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) i64 (listof char acyclic)) string)
    (lambda (cs n acc)
      (cond ((null? cs) (list->string (reverse acc)))
            ((char=? (car cs) #\}) (str-unescaped (cdr cs) (cons (i64->char n) acc)))
            (else (let ((k (char->i64 (car cs))))
                    (str-code (cdr cs) (i64+ (i64* n 16) (if (i64< k 58) (i64- k 48) (i64- k 87))) acc)))))))

"A string at `i` (its opening quote): itself, its text as written, and where
 it ends."
(define sc-str (subr kfx (string i64 i64 amap) part)
  (lambda (s i n atoms)
    (tagcase (sc-str-end s (i64+ i 1) n 0)
      (scanned (esc e)
        (let ((inner (substring s (i64->int (i64+ i 1)) (i64->int e))))
          (part (str (if (i64= esc 1) (str-unescaped (string-chars inner) nil) inner) "" 0)
                (substring s (i64->int i) (i64->int (i64+ e 1)))
                atoms (i64+ e 1)))))))

(define-rec
  (sc-name-end (subr kfx (string i64 i64) i64)
    (lambda (s i n) (let ((c (sc-char s i n))) (if (or (i64< c 0) (i64= c 32) (i64= c 10) (i64= c 40) (i64= c 41)) i (sc-name-end s (i64+ i 1) n))))))

(define-rec
  (sc-part (subr kfx (string i64 i64 amap) part)
    (lambda (s i n atoms)
      "One part of a key: a string, labelled where first written and named by
       its label after; a number; or a name."
      (let* ((i (sc-ws s i n)) (c (sc-char s i n)))
        (cond ((i64= c 35)
               (tagcase (sc-digits s (i64+ i 1) n 0)
                 (scanned (k e)
                   (if (i64= (sc-char s e n) 61)
                       (tagcase (sc-part s (i64+ e 1) n atoms)
                         (part (x t atoms2 e2) (part x t (am-put atoms2 k (atom x t)) e2)))
                       (let ((found (am-get atoms k)))
                         (if (null? found)
                             (begin (error "kayak-db: a label no part made") (part (sym "" "" 0) "" atoms (i64+ e 1)))
                             (tagcase (car found) (atom (x t) (part x t atoms (i64+ e 1))))))))))
              ((i64= c 34) (sc-str s i n atoms))
              ((or (i64= c 45) (and (i64>= c 48) (i64<= c 57)))
               (tagcase (sc-int s i n) (scanned (v e) (part (num v "" 0) (substring s (i64->int i) (i64->int e)) atoms e))))
              (else
               (let ((e (sc-name-end s i n)))
                 (let ((t (substring s (i64->int i) (i64->int e)))) (part (sym t "" 0) t atoms e))))))))
  (sc-parts (subr kfx (string i64 i64 amap sexps (listof string acyclic)) parts)
    (lambda (s i n atoms xs ts)
      "A key's parts to its `)`, the newest first."
      (let ((i (sc-ws s i n)))
        (if (i64= (sc-char s i n) 41)
            (parts xs ts atoms (i64+ i 1))
            (tagcase (sc-part s i n atoms)
              (part (x t atoms2 e) (sc-parts s e n atoms2 (cons x xs) (cons t ts)))))))))

(define-rec
  (texts-spaced (subr kfx ((listof string acyclic) (listof string acyclic)) (listof string acyclic))
    (lambda (ts acc) (if (null? ts) acc (texts-spaced (cdr ts) (cons (car ts) (if (null? acc) acc (cons " " acc))))))))

(define-rec
  (keys-scanned! (subr qe (db string i64 i64 amap i64) scanned)
    (lambda (d s i n atoms top)
      "Each record `(LEN #N=(KEY ...))` of the keys, to its `)`; the greatest
       number, and where the keys end."
      (let ((i (sc-ws s i n)))
        (if (not (i64= (sc-char s i n) 40))
            (scanned top (i64+ i 1))
            (tagcase (sc-int s (i64+ i 1) n)
              (scanned (len b)
                (let* ((b (i64+ b 1)) (after (i64+ b len)))
                  (tagcase (sc-digits s (i64+ b 1) n 0)
                    (scanned (k e)
                      (tagcase (sc-parts s (i64+ e 2) n atoms nil nil)
                        (parts (xs ts atoms2 e2)
                          (let ((key (lst (reverse xs) "" 0 0))
                                (text (string-append "(" (string-append (string-list-append (texts-spaced ts nil)) ")"))))
                            (begin
                              (set (extract d ids) (km-put (get (extract d ids)) text k))
                              (set (extract d nodes) (im-put (get (extract d nodes)) k (node key #f -1 -1 0 nil 0 (v-none))))
                              (keys-scanned! d s after n atoms2 (if (i64> k top) k top))))))))))))))))

(define-rec
  (nodes-scanned! (subr qe (db string i64 i64) unit)
    (lambda (d s i n)
      "Each record of the nodes, to their `)`: its offset noted in its key's
       node, the record stepped over by its length, not read (C417)."
      (let ((i (sc-ws s i n)))
        (if (not (i64= (sc-char s i n) 40))
            #u
            (tagcase (sc-int s (i64+ i 1) n)
              (scanned (len b)
                (tagcase (sc-digits s (i64+ b 2) n 0)
                  (scanned (k e)
                    (let ((x (car (im-get (get (extract d nodes)) k))))
                      (begin
                        (set (extract d nodes) (im-put (get (extract d nodes)) k (node (node-key x) #f -1 i 0 nil 0 (v-none))))
                        (nodes-scanned! d s (i64+ (i64+ b 1) len) n))))))))))))

"A value file's text if its fingerprint is `fp`; else none (C472): a
 file cut short, or written after the graph that names it was (a save cut
 short), is not believed."
(define value-checked (subr kfx (string i64) (listof string acyclic))
  (lambda (x fp) (if (i64= ((with queries fnv-string) x (with queries fnv-offset)) fp) (list x) nil)))

"Where a shard's values begin in its file's text (C473): after its first
 line, `(kayak-shard 3 NEXT LENGTH)`."
(define shard-values-start (subr kfx (string) i64)
  (lambda (t) (i64+ (sc-close t 0 (string-length-i64 t)) 2)))

;;; ------------------------------------------------------------ the shards


"A key's group, which its shard is of (C472): its first argument, a
 file's path for most of kc's queries, so that one program's nodes are in
 one shard, and a run reads the shards of what it reads; else its query's
 name. And the group's hash, by which the head names its shard."
(define key-group (subr kfx (sexp) string)
  (lambda (k) (let ((a (key-arg k 0))) (if (string=? a "") (key-query k) a))))
(define group-hash (subr kfx (string) string)
  (lambda (g) (i64->string ((with queries fnv-string) g (with queries fnv-offset)))))

(define shard-text (subr kfx (shard) string) (lambda (x) (tagcase x (shard (h slot text next loaded dirty) text))))

(define sm-height (subr kfx (smap) i64) (lambda (t) (tagcase t (sm-none () 0) (sm-node (l k x h r) h))))
(define sm-make (subr kfx (smap i64 shard smap) smap)
  (lambda (l k x r) (sm-node l k x (i64+ 1 (let ((a (sm-height l)) (b (sm-height r))) (if (i64> a b) a b))) r)))
(define sm-balanced (subr kfx (smap i64 shard smap) smap)
  (lambda (l k x r)
    (let ((hl (sm-height l)) (hr (sm-height r)))
      (cond ((i64> hl (i64+ hr 1))
             (tagcase l
               (sm-node (ll lk lx lh lr)
                 (if (i64>= (sm-height ll) (sm-height lr))
                     (sm-make ll lk lx (sm-make lr k x r))
                     (tagcase lr (sm-node (rl rk rx rh rr) (sm-make (sm-make ll lk lx rl) rk rx (sm-make rr k x r))) (sm-none () (sm-make l k x r)))))
               (sm-none () (sm-make l k x r))))
            ((i64> hr (i64+ hl 1))
             (tagcase r
               (sm-node (rl rk rx rh rr)
                 (if (i64>= (sm-height rr) (sm-height rl))
                     (sm-make (sm-make l k x rl) rk rx rr)
                     (tagcase rl (sm-node (ml mk mx mh mr) (sm-make (sm-make l k x ml) mk mx (sm-make mr rk rx rr))) (sm-none () (sm-make l k x r)))))
               (sm-none () (sm-make l k x r))))
            (else (sm-make l k x r))))))
(define-rec
  (sm-put (subr kfx (smap i64 shard) smap)
    (lambda (t n x)
      (tagcase t
        (sm-none () (sm-node (sm-none) n x 1 (sm-none)))
        (sm-node (l k y h r)
          (cond ((i64= n k) (sm-node l k x h r))
                ((i64< n k) (sm-balanced (sm-put l n x) k y r))
                (else (sm-balanced l k y (sm-put r n x))))))))
  (sm-get (subr kfx (smap i64) (listof shard acyclic))
    (lambda (t n)
      (tagcase t
        (sm-none () nil)
        (sm-node (l k x h r) (cond ((i64= n k) (list x)) ((i64< n k) (sm-get l n)) (else (sm-get r n))))))))

(define sm-set! (subr qe (db i64 shard) unit)
  (lambda (d n x) (set (extract d shards) (sm-put (get (extract d shards)) n x))))

"Shard `n`, which the database has (each number made is of one)."
(define db-shard (subr qe (db i64) shard)
  (lambda (d n)
    (let ((x (sm-get (get (extract d shards)) n)))
      (if (null? x) (begin (error "kayak-db: no such shard") (shard "" -1 "" 0 #t #f)) (car x)))))

(define shard-file (subr kfx (i64 i64) string)
  (lambda (n slot) (string-append "g" (string-append (i64->string n) (string-append "." (i64->string slot))))))
(define value-file (subr kfx (i64) string) (lambda (i) (string-append "v" (i64->string i))))

"Shard `n` read, if the database has it and it is not yet (C472): its
 file's keys numbered, its nodes' records noted, read when asked for. A
 file not there, or not a shard's, has nothing: its numbers stay its own
 (its next number the head's), so that none is given to another key, and
 what read one of them runs again."
(define db-shard-read! (subr qe (db i64) unit)
  (lambda (d n)
    (let ((x (sm-get (get (extract d shards)) n)))
      (if (null? x)
          #u
          (tagcase (car x)
            (shard (h slot text0 next loaded dirty)
              (if loaded
                  #u
                  (let* ((text (if (i64< slot 0) "" ((get (extract d reads)) (shard-file n slot))))
                         (m (string-length-i64 text))
                         (hd "(kayak-shard 3 ")
                         (ok (and (i64> m (string-length-i64 hd)) (string=? (substring text 0 (string-length hd)) hd))))
                    (begin
                      (sm-set! d n (shard h slot (if ok text "") next #t dirty))
                      (if ok
                          ;; Its values (C473), then `(keys`.
                          (let ((k0 (sc-ws text (i64+ (shard-values-start text) (db-nth (sc-ints text (string-length-i64 hd) m 2 nil) 1)) m)))
                            ;; `(keys`, then its records; `(nodes`, then theirs.
                            (tagcase (keys-scanned! d text (i64+ k0 5) m (am-none) -1)
                              (scanned (top e) (nodes-scanned! d text (i64+ (sc-ws text e m) 6) m))))
                          #u))))))))))

"The shard of group `g`, read; a new one if the database has none."
(define db-shard-of-group! (subr qe (db string) i64)
  (lambda (d g)
    (let* ((h (group-hash g)) (n (km-get (get (extract d groups)) h)))
      (if (i64>= n 0)
          (begin (db-shard-read! d n) n)
          (let ((m (get (extract d nshards))))
            (begin
              (set (extract d nshards) (i64+ m 1))
              (set (extract d groups) (km-put (get (extract d groups)) h m))
              (sm-set! d m (shard h -1 "" 0 #t #f))
              m))))))

"Node `i`'s value read from its file, if it is there unread: as it was
 made, or none if the file is not as the graph says (`value-checked`), so
 that it is made again."
(define db-node-read! (subr qe (db i64) unit)
  (lambda (d i)
    (let ((n (im-get (get (extract d nodes)) i)))
      (if (null? n)
          #u
          (tagcase (node-kept (car n))
            (v-file (j)
              (let ((x (value-checked ((get (extract d reads)) (value-file i)) (node-fp (car n)))))
                (tagcase (car n)
                  (node (k inp v c f ds du val)
                    (set (extract d nodes) (im-put (get (extract d nodes)) i (node k inp v c f ds du (if (null? x) (v-none) (v-read (car x))))))))))
            (else other #u))))))

;;; ------------------------------------------------------------ the database

(define db-make (subr qe () db)
  (lambda ()
    (product (rev (the (ref i64 @q) (new 1)))
             (nodes (the (ref imap @q) (new (im-none))))
             (ids (the (ref kmap @q) (new (km-none))))
             (shards (the (ref smap @q) (new (sm-none))))
             (groups (the (ref kmap @q) (new (km-none))))
             (nshards (the (ref i64 @q) (new 0)))
             (reads (the (ref reader @q) (new (lambda ((name string)) ""))))
             (dirty (the (ref bool @q) (new #f)))
             (frames (the (ref (listof frame acyclic) @q) (new nil)))
             (last (the (ref (listof i64 acyclic) @q) (new (zeros durabilities))))
             (runs (the (ref i64 @q) (new 0)))
             (ran (the (ref sexps @q) (new nil))))))

(define db-revision (subr qe (db) i64) (lambda (d) (get (extract d rev))))
(define db-runs (subr qe (db) i64) (lambda (d) (get (extract d runs))))
"The keys whose bodies ran, the newest first: so that a test can say what
 an edit made run again, and what it spared."
(define db-ran (subr qe (db) sexps) (lambda (d) (get (extract d ran))))

"A key's number (C472): its shard's, read first if it is not; made, in its
 shard, the first time the key is met."
(define db-id (subr qe (db sexp) i64)
  (lambda (d k)
    (let* ((t (key-text k)) (i (km-get (get (extract d ids)) t)))
      (if (i64>= i 0)
          i
          (let* ((s (db-shard-of-group! d (key-group k)))
                 (j (km-get (get (extract d ids)) t)))
            (if (i64>= j 0)
                j
                (tagcase (db-shard d s)
                  (shard (h slot text next loaded dirty)
                    (let ((n (i64+ (i64* s shard-span) next)))
                      (begin
                        (sm-set! d s (shard h slot text (i64+ next 1) loaded dirty))
                        (set (extract d ids) (km-put (get (extract d ids)) t n))
                        n))))))))))

"A node by number; one read with the database but not yet looked at (its
 record noted, C417: its revision verified -1, its record's offset in the
 graph as its revision of change) read from its record the first time it is
 asked for; one whose key has no record, none."
(define db-node-at (subr qe (db i64) (listof node acyclic))
  (lambda (d i)
    (let ((n (begin (db-shard-read! d (shard-of-number i)) (im-get (get (extract d nodes)) i))))
      (if (or (null? n) (not (i64= (node-verified (car n)) -1)))
          n
          (if (i64< (node-changed (car n)) 0)
              nil
              (let ((x (node-record (shard-text (db-shard d (shard-of-number i))) (node-changed (car n)) (node-key (car n)))))
                (begin
                  (set (extract d nodes) (im-put (get (extract d nodes)) i x))
                  (list x))))))))

(define db-node (subr qe (db sexp) (listof node acyclic))
  (lambda (d k) (db-node-at d (db-id d k))))

(define db-put! (subr qe (db i64 node) unit)
  (lambda (d i n)
    (begin
      (set (extract d dirty) #t)
      (tagcase (db-shard d (shard-of-number i))
        (shard (h slot text next loaded dirty) (sm-set! d (shard-of-number i) (shard h slot text next loaded #t))))
      (set (extract d nodes) (im-put (get (extract d nodes)) i n)))))

"Whether a node has changed since the database was made or read: if not,
 its files are as they were, and need not be written (C417)."
"What reads the database's files (C472)."
(define db-reader (subr qe (db) reader) (lambda (d) (get (extract d reads))))

(define db-dirty? (subr qe (db) bool) (lambda (d) (get (extract d dirty))))

(define-rec
  (ascii-escaped (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) (listof string acyclic)) (listof string acyclic))
    (lambda (cs acc)
      "A value's characters as the payload keeps them, the newest first."
      (if (null? cs)
          acc
          (let ((k (char->i64 (car cs))))
            (ascii-escaped (cdr cs)
                           (cons (cond ((char=? (car cs) #\\) "\\\\")
                                       ((i64> k 127) (string-append "\\u{" (string-append (hex-of k "") "}")))
                                       (else (list->string (list (car cs)))))
                                 acc)))))))

(define-rec
  (ascii-only? (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic)) bool)
    (lambda (cs) (cond ((null? cs) #t) ((i64> (char->i64 (car cs)) 127) #f) (else (ascii-only? (cdr cs)))))))

(define payload-text (subr kfx (string) string)
  (lambda (x) (if (ascii-only? (string-chars x)) x (string-list-append (reverse (ascii-escaped (string-chars x) nil))))))

(define-rec
  (ascii-unescaped (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) (listof char acyclic)) string)
    (lambda (cs acc)
      (cond ((null? cs) (list->string (reverse acc)))
            ((and (char=? (car cs) #\\) (not (null? (cdr cs))) (char=? (car (cdr cs)) #\\)) (ascii-unescaped (cdr (cdr cs)) (cons #\\ acc)))
            ((and (char=? (car cs) #\\) (not (null? (cdr cs))) (char=? (car (cdr cs)) #\u))
             (ascii-code (cdr (cdr (cdr cs))) 0 acc))
            (else (ascii-unescaped (cdr cs) (cons (car cs) acc))))))
  (ascii-code (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) i64 (listof char acyclic)) string)
    (lambda (cs n acc)
      (cond ((null? cs) (list->string (reverse acc)))
            ((char=? (car cs) #\}) (ascii-unescaped (cdr cs) (cons (i64->char n) acc)))
            (else (let ((k (char->i64 (car cs))))
                    (ascii-code (cdr cs) (i64+ (i64* n 16) (if (i64< k 58) (i64- k 48) (i64- k 87))) acc)))))))

"A node's value as text: kept, read from its file or its shard's, or `` if
 none is kept (a reader makes it again first, `db-node-read!`)."
(define node-value-in (subr qe (db node) string)
  (lambda (d n)
    (tagcase (node-kept n)
      (v-text (s) s)
      (v-read (s) s)
      (v-file (i)
        (let ((x (value-checked ((get (extract d reads)) (value-file i)) (node-fp n))))
          (if (null? x) "" (car x))))
      (v-at (sh o len esc)
        (let* ((t (shard-text (db-shard d sh)))
               (b (i64+ (shard-values-start t) o))
               (x (substring t (i64->int b) (i64->int (i64+ b len)))))
          (if esc (ascii-unescaped (string-chars x) nil) x)))
      (v-none () ""))))

(define node-value (subr qe (db node) string)
  (lambda (d n) (node-value-in d n)))

"A side store (C415): text kept with the database under a name, no
 query's input and no query's value: no revision for it, nothing depends
 on it. For what is content-addressed, whose use can spare work and change
 no value (the checker's memos, each keyed by a fingerprint of all it was
 made from); kept as the nodes are, under the key `(%side NAME)`, and so
 written and read with them."
(define db-side (subr qe (db string) string)
  (lambda (d k)
    (let ((n (db-node d (key1 "%side" k))))
      (if (null? n) "" (node-value-in d (car n))))))

(define db-side-put! (subr qe (db string string) unit)
  (lambda (d k text)
    (let ((key (key1 "%side" k)))
      ;; Its fingerprint its text's (C473): a value read from a file is
      ;; believed only if its fingerprint is the graph's.
      (db-put! d (db-id d key) (node key #t 0 0 ((with queries fnv-string) text (with queries fnv-offset)) nil 0 (v-text text))))))

"Input `k` set to `text`, of durability `du`: a new revision if its value
 is new. Of a key no node is of (C449), no new revision: nothing has read
 it, so no value made is made stale, and a query may make inputs no one
 has asked for (a transformer's phase-1 file, `phase1 REQUEST`) without
 sending every node to be verified again. Not in `models/db.qnt` yet,
 whose inputs all are from the first."
(define db-set! (subr qe (db sexp string i64) unit)
  (lambda (d k text du)
    (let* ((fp ((with queries fnv-string) text (with queries fnv-offset)))
           (i (db-id d k))
           (old (db-node-at d i)))
      (cond
        ((and (not (null? old)) (node-input? (car old)) (i64= (node-fp (car old)) fp) (i64= (node-durability (car old)) du))
         #u)
        ((null? old)
         (let ((r (get (extract d rev))))
           (db-put! d i (node k #t r r fp nil du (v-text text)))))
        (else
          (let ((r (i64+ (get (extract d rev)) 1)))
            (begin
              (set (extract d rev) r)
              ;; At the higher of its durabilities, old and new: what read it
              ;; when it was of the old one counts on that (C399, found by
              ;; `db-verify`).
              (set (extract d last) (bumped (get (extract d last))
                                            (if (and (not (null? old)) (i64> (node-durability (car old)) du)) (node-durability (car old)) du)
                                            r 0))
              (db-put! d i (node k #t r r fp nil du (v-text text))))))))))

"That the innermost query being run read `i`, of durability `du`."
(define note-read! (subr qe (db i64 i64) unit)
  (lambda (d i du)
    (let ((fs (get (extract d frames))))
      (if (null? fs)
          #u
          (tagcase (car fs)
            (frame (fk ds fdu)
              (set (extract d frames) (cons (frame fk (cons i ds) (if (i64< du fdu) du fdu)) (cdr fs)))))))))

(define-rec
  (db-get (subr qe (db runner sexp) string)
    (lambda (d run k)
      "`k`'s value, current, and that the query being run read it."
      (let ((i (db-id d k)))
        (if (id-in? i (get (extract d frames)))
            (begin (error (string-append "a cycle of queries, through " (key-text k))) "")
            (let ((x (db-current d run i k)))
              (begin
                (note-read! d i (let ((n (db-node-at d i))) (if (null? n) 0 (node-durability (car n)))))
                x))))))

  (db-current (subr qe (db runner i64 sexp) string)
    (lambda (d run i k)
      "`k`'s value, made current (`db-made-current`); one of a query whose
       value was not kept (C417) made again: its fingerprint the one it had,
       nothing that read it runs."
      (begin
        (db-made-current d run i k)
        (db-node-read! d i)
        (let ((n (db-node-at d i)))
          (if (node-has-value? (car n)) (node-value-in d (car n)) (db-execute d run i k n))))))

  (db-made-current (subr qe (db runner i64 sexp) unit)
    (lambda (d run i k)
      "`k` made current, its value not read: an input as set; a query
       verified, or run again."
      (let ((old (db-node-at d i)) (r (get (extract d rev))))
        (cond ((null? old) (begin (db-execute d run i k old) #u))
              ((node-input? (car old)) #u)
              ((i64= (node-verified (car old)) r) #u)
              ((i64<= (db-nth (get (extract d last)) (node-durability (car old))) (node-verified (car old)))
               (db-put! d i (node-verified-at (car old) r)))
              (else
               ;; Its reads, each made current in order: if none changed after
               ;; it was verified, it is current, its least durability theirs
               ;; as they are now (an input's lowered durability may have
               ;; lowered it: found by `models/db.qnt`, C400).
               (let ((du (db-reads-durability d run (node-deps (car old)) (node-verified (car old)) (i64- durabilities 1))))
                 (if (i64>= du 0)
                     (db-put! d i (node-reverified (car old) r du))
                     (begin (db-execute d run i k old) #u))))))))

  (db-reads-durability (subr qe (db runner (listof i64 acyclic) i64 i64) i64)
    (lambda (d run is since du)
      "If none of `is`, each made current in turn, changed after `since`,
       their least durability, and `du`'s; else -1, at the first that did."
      (if (null? is)
          du
          (let ((n0 (db-node-at d (car is))))
            (if (null? n0)
                -1
                (begin
                  ;; Made current, its value not read (C417): what a node read
                  ;; is verified by revisions and fingerprints alone.
                  (db-made-current d run (car is) (node-key (car n0)))
                  (let ((n (db-node-at d (car is))))
                    (if (or (null? n) (i64> (node-changed (car n)) since))
                        -1
                        (db-reads-durability d run (cdr is) since (if (i64< (node-durability (car n)) du) (node-durability (car n)) du))))))))))

  (db-execute (subr qe (db runner i64 sexp (listof node acyclic)) string)
    (lambda (d run i k old)
      "`k`'s query run, its reads recorded; its value's fingerprint the
       same as `old`'s, its revision of change kept (early cutoff)."
      (begin
        (set (extract d frames) (cons (frame i nil (i64- durabilities 1)) (get (extract d frames))))
        (let* ((x (run d k))
               (fr (car (get (extract d frames))))
               (r (get (extract d rev)))
               (fp ((with queries fnv-string) x (with queries fnv-offset))))
          (begin
            (set (extract d frames) (cdr (get (extract d frames))))
            (set (extract d runs) (i64+ (get (extract d runs)) 1))
            (set (extract d ran) (cons k (get (extract d ran))))
            (tagcase fr
              (frame (fk ds du)
                (db-put! d i (node k #f r (if (and (not (null? old)) (i64= (node-fp (car old)) fp)) (node-changed (car old)) r)
                                   fp (reverse ds) du (v-text x)))))
            x))))))

"`k` made current, its value's fingerprint, and that the query being run
 read it (C418): a reader of a fingerprint is run again when it changes,
 as a reader of a value is when that does, the two changing together (a
 node's revision of change moves when its fingerprint does, early cutoff);
 the value neither read nor made. For a query of what has been made by
 name of its content (`kc build`'s objects)."
(define db-get-fingerprint (subr qe (db runner sexp) i64)
  (lambda (d run k)
    (let ((i (db-id d k)))
      (if (id-in? i (get (extract d frames)))
          (begin (error (string-append "a cycle of queries, through " (key-text k))) 0)
          (begin
            (db-made-current d run i k)
            (let ((n (car (db-node-at d i))))
              (begin (note-read! d i (node-durability n)) (node-fp n))))))))

"`k` made current, and its value's fingerprint, its value neither read nor
 made (C417): so that a client holding a value already (a file it wrote)
 may know it is as it was."
(define db-fingerprint (subr qe (db runner sexp) i64)
  (lambda (d run k)
    (let ((i (db-id d k)))
      (begin (db-made-current d run i k) (node-fp (car (db-node-at d i)))))))

;;; ------------------------------------------------------------ as files

"The database as files (C472, `kayak-db 3`; C417's two, read and written
 whole, before): a run reads what it reads, and writes what changed.

 - the head, its name ``: `(kayak-db 3 WHOSE REVISION (LAST ...) ((HASH
   SLOT NEXT) ...))`, whose it is (a compiler's identity), the
   durabilities' revisions, and each shard, by number, its group's hash,
   the slot its file is in, and its next number;
 - a shard's file, `gN.SLOT`: `(kayak-shard 3 NEXT LENGTH)`, then its
   values of `inline-most` characters or fewer (C473), one after another,
   `LENGTH` in all, each written with each `\` `\\` and each character
   past ASCII `\u{HEX}` if it has one past ASCII, and marked so; then
   `(keys #I=KEY ...)`, each key labelled by its number where it is written, each text
   in them written more than once (a path) labelled where first written;
   then `(nodes (#I# INPUT VERIFIED CHANGED FINGERPRINT DURABILITY (#M#
   ...) VALUE) ...)`, each node's key and what it read by number, its
   value `(at OFFSET LENGTH)` (or `atx`, escaped) in the shard's values,
   `file`, or `none`; each record `(LEN ...)`, stepped over unread
   until its node is asked for (C417). ASCII alone, so that an offset is a
   character's. A shard of which a node changed is written to the other
   of its two slots, and the head, written last, names the slot: a save
   cut short leaves the files the old head names as they were;
 - a longer value's file, `vI`, its node's number: its text, as it is,
   read when it is asked for and believed if its fingerprint is the
   graph's. Small values are not files of their own, since each file
   written is flushed to the disk (FX-26's `write-file`, C473).

 A key whose value `keep` says is not to be kept (a whole program's output,
 made again from its parts, which are kept) is written `none`: its node,
 fingerprint and reads are kept, so that it is verified as any is, and
 made again only when its value is read."
(define db-format string "kayak-db 3")

"A file to write: its name, and its text."
(define-datatype db-file (db-file string string))

(define-datatype keyed-out (keyed-out (listof string acyclic) kmap i64))

(define-rec
  (key-written (subr kfx (sexp kmap i64 (listof string acyclic)) keyed-out)
    (lambda (k seen n acc)
      "Key `k` as text onto `acc` (newest first), each text in it seen
       before by its label, each seen first labelled, from `n`."
      (tagcase k
        (str (s f p)
          (let ((j (km-get seen s)))
            (if (i64>= j 0)
                (keyed-out (cons (string-append "#" (string-append (i64->string j) "#")) acc) seen n)
                (keyed-out (cons (str-text s) (cons (string-append "#" (string-append (i64->string n) "=")) acc)) (km-put seen s n) (i64+ n 1)))))
        (lst (xs f l p)
          (tagcase (keys-written xs seen n (cons "(" acc))
            (keyed-out (acc2 seen2 n2) (keyed-out (cons ")" acc2) seen2 n2))))
        (else other (keyed-out (cons (key-text k) acc) seen n)))))
  (keys-written (subr kfx (sexps kmap i64 (listof string acyclic)) keyed-out)
    (lambda (xs seen n acc)
      (if (null? xs)
          (keyed-out acc seen n)
          (tagcase (key-written (car xs) seen n acc)
            (keyed-out (acc2 seen2 n2)
              (keys-written (cdr xs) seen2 n2 (if (null? (cdr xs)) acc2 (cons " " acc2)))))))))

(define-rec
  (labels-text (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic) (listof string acyclic)) (listof string acyclic))
    (lambda (is acc)
      (if (null? is)
          acc
          (labels-text (cdr is) (cons (string-append "#" (string-append (i64->string (car is)) "#")) (if (null? acc) acc (cons " " acc))))))))

"A record of a shard (C417): `(LEN ...)`, `LEN` the length of what follows
 it and its space, to the record's `)`, so that a reader may step over it
 unread: `body` is that, its `)` included."
(define length-first (subr kfx (string) string)
  (lambda (body) (string-append "\n (" (string-append (i64->string (string-length-i64 body)) (string-append " " body)))))

"A shard's records made: its keys', its nodes', the values' files to
 write; the texts seen in keys, and the next label."
"The most characters a value kept in its shard's file has (C473): one
 longer is a file of its own, as the expander's maker's code is; one so
 short is not, since each file written is flushed to the disk (FX-26's
 `write-file`), which a cold build of a program of a thousand procedures,
 a file a value, paid five seconds for."
(define inline-most i64 4096)

"A shard's records made: its keys', its nodes', the values' own files to
 write, and its values kept in it, the newest first; the texts seen in
 keys, the next label, and the values' length so far."
(define-datatype made-files (made-files (listof string acyclic) (listof string acyclic) (listof db-file acyclic) (listof string acyclic) kmap i64 i64))

"Where a node's value goes: in the shard, its text as there and whether
 escaped; in a file of its own, a new one's text to write, or none (it is
 there); or nowhere."
(define-datatype placed (in-shard string bool) (in-file (listof string acyclic)) (nowhere))

(define value-placed (subr qe (db node bool) placed)
  (lambda (d n kept)
    (if (not kept)
        (nowhere)
        (tagcase (node-kept n)
          (v-none () (nowhere))
          (v-file (i) (in-file nil))
          (v-read (t) (in-file nil))
          (v-at (sh o l e)
            (let* ((t (shard-text (db-shard d sh))) (b (i64+ (shard-values-start t) o)))
              (in-shard (substring t (i64->int b) (i64->int (i64+ b l))) e)))
          (v-text (t)
            (if (i64> (string-length-i64 t) inline-most)
                (in-file (list t))
                (in-shard (payload-text t) (not (ascii-only? (string-chars t))))))))))

(define-rec
  (nodes-files (subr qe (db i64 (listof i64 acyclic) (subr kfx (sexp) bool) made-files) made-files)
    (lambda (d sh is keep m)
      "Each node of shard `sh` of `is`, its key into the keys, its record
       into the nodes, its value into the shard's values or a file of its
       own (C473), and as they have it after."
      (if (null? is)
          m
          (tagcase m
            (made-files (keys nodes files payload seen labels at)
              (if (null? (db-node-at d (car is)))
                  (nodes-files d sh (cdr is) keep m)
              (let ((n (car (db-node-at d (car is)))))
                (tagcase (key-written (node-key n) seen labels (list (string-append "#" (string-append (i64->string (car is)) "="))))
                  (keyed-out (key-parts seen2 labels2)
                    (let* ((p (value-placed d n (or (node-input? n) (keep (node-key n)))))
                           (after (tagcase p
                                    (in-shard (raw e) (list (v-at sh at (string-length-i64 raw) e)))
                                    (in-file (ts) (if (null? ts) nil (list (v-read (car ts)))))
                                    (nowhere () nil)))
                           (said (tagcase p
                                   (in-shard (raw e) (string-list-append (list (if e "(atx " "(at ") (i64->string at) " " (i64->string (string-length-i64 raw)) ")")))
                                   (in-file (ts) "file")
                                   (nowhere () "none"))))
                      (begin
                        (if (null? after)
                            #u
                            (tagcase n
                              (node (k inp v c f ds du val)
                                (set (extract d nodes) (im-put (get (extract d nodes)) (car is) (node k inp v c f ds du (car after)))))))
                        (nodes-files d sh (cdr is) keep
                          (made-files (cons (length-first (string-append (string-list-append (reverse key-parts)) ")")) keys)
                                      (cons (length-first (string-list-append
                                              (list "#" (i64->string (car is)) "# " (if (node-input? n) "1 " "0 ")
                                                    (i64->string (node-verified n)) " " (i64->string (node-changed n)) " "
                                                    (i64->string (node-fp n)) " " (i64->string (node-durability n)) " ("
                                                    (string-list-append (reverse (labels-text (node-deps n) nil))) ") "
                                                    said ")")))
                                            nodes)
                                      (tagcase p
                                        (in-file (ts) (if (null? ts) files (cons (db-file (value-file (car is)) (car ts)) files)))
                                        (else other files))
                                      (tagcase p (in-shard (raw e) (cons raw payload)) (else other payload))
                                      seen2 labels2
                                      (tagcase p (in-shard (raw e) (i64+ at (string-length-i64 raw))) (else other at))))))))))))))))

(define-rec
  (numbers-text (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic)) (listof string acyclic))
    (lambda (xs) (if (null? xs) nil (cons " " (cons (i64->string (car xs)) (numbers-text (cdr xs))))))))

(define-rec
  (numbers-from (subr kfx (i64 i64 i64 (listof i64 acyclic)) (listof i64 acyclic))
    (lambda (base k n acc) (if (i64>= k n) (reverse acc) (numbers-from base (i64+ k 1) n (cons (i64+ base k) acc))))))

(define-rec
  (sm-numbers (subr kfx (smap (listof i64 acyclic)) (listof i64 acyclic))
    (lambda (t acc) (tagcase t (sm-none () acc) (sm-node (l k x h r) (sm-numbers l (cons k (sm-numbers r acc))))))))

(define-rec
  (shards-saved (subr qe (db (listof i64 acyclic) (subr kfx (sexp) bool) (listof db-file acyclic) (listof db-file acyclic) (listof string acyclic))
                      (tupleof (listof db-file acyclic) (listof db-file acyclic) (listof string acyclic)))
    (lambda (d ns keep values graphs heads)
      "Each shard of `ns`: if a node of it changed, its file written to its
       other slot, and its values' files; its line of the head."
      (if (null? ns)
          (tuple values graphs (reverse heads))
          (tagcase (db-shard d (car ns))
            (shard (h slot text next loaded dirty)
              (if (not dirty)
                  (shards-saved d (cdr ns) keep values graphs
                                (cons (string-list-append (list " (" h " " (i64->string slot) " " (i64->string next) ")")) heads))
                  (tagcase (nodes-files d (car ns) (numbers-from (i64* (car ns) shard-span) 0 next nil) keep (made-files nil nil nil nil (km-none) 0 0))
                    (made-files (keys nodes files payload seen labels at)
                      (let* ((to (if (i64= slot 0) (the i64 1) (the i64 0)))
                             (t (string-list-append
                                  (append (list "(kayak-shard 3 " (i64->string next) " " (i64->string at) ")\n" (string-list-append (reverse payload)) "\n(keys")
                                    (append (reverse keys)
                                      (append (list ")\n(nodes") (append (reverse nodes) (list ")\n"))))))))
                        (begin
                          (sm-set! d (car ns) (shard h to t next #t #f))
                          (shards-saved d (cdr ns) keep (onto (reverse files) values)
                                        (cons (db-file (shard-file (car ns) to) t) graphs)
                                        (cons (string-list-append (list " (" h " " (i64->string to) " " (i64->string next) ")")) heads)))))))))))))

"The files to write of what changed since the database was read or last
 saved, `whose` it is, `keep` saying of a query's key whether its value is
 kept, in the order to write them: the values', the shards', the head
 last. Its nodes after are as those files have them."
(define db-saved (subr qe (db string (subr kfx (sexp) bool)) (listof db-file acyclic))
  (lambda (d whose keep)
    (let ((r (shards-saved d (sm-numbers (get (extract d shards)) nil) keep nil nil nil)))
      (begin
        (set (extract d dirty) #f)
        (onto (extract r 1)
              (onto (extract r 2)
                    (list (db-file ""
                                   (string-list-append
                                     (append (list "(" db-format " " (str-text whose) " " (i64->string (get (extract d rev))) " (")
                                       (append (cdr (numbers-text (get (extract d last))))
                                         (append (list ") (") (append (extract r 3) (list "))\n"))))))))))))))

(define-rec
  (shards-scanned! (subr qe (db string i64 i64 i64) unit)
    (lambda (d s i n k)
      "The head's shards, `(HASH SLOT NEXT)` each, numbered from `k`, none
       read yet."
      (let ((i (sc-ws s i n)))
        (if (not (i64= (sc-char s i n) 40))
            (set (extract d nshards) k)
            (let ((xs (sc-ints s (i64+ i 1) n 3 nil)))
              (let ((h (i64->string (db-nth xs 0))))
                (begin
                  (set (extract d groups) (km-put (get (extract d groups)) h k))
                  (sm-set! d k (shard h (db-nth xs 1) "" (db-nth xs 2) #f #f))
                  (shards-scanned! d s (i64+ (sc-close s (db-nth xs 3) n) 1) n (i64+ k 1))))))))))

(define db-opened (subr qe (reader string) db)
  (lambda (rd whose)
    "The database whose files `rd` reads, if its head says it is `whose`;
     else an empty one, as files of another format, or another's, have
     none for this (C472). Its shards read as their keys are asked for."
    (let* ((d (db-make))
           (graph (begin (set (extract d reads) rd) (rd "")))
           (h (string-append "(" (string-append db-format " ")))
           (n (string-length-i64 graph))
           (hn (string-length-i64 h)))
      (if (not (and (i64>= n hn) (string=? (substring graph 0 (i64->int hn)) h) (i64= (sc-char graph hn n) 34)))
          d
          (tagcase (sc-str graph hn n (am-none))
            (part (w wt atoms e)
              (if (not (tagcase w (str (t f p) (string=? t whose)) (else other #f)))
                  d
                  (let* ((ns (sc-ints graph e n 1 nil))
                         (lasts (sc-ints graph (i64+ (sc-ws graph (db-nth ns 1) n) 1) n durabilities nil))
                         (at (sc-ws graph (i64+ (sc-close graph (db-nth lasts durabilities) n) 1) n)))
                    (begin
                      (set (extract d rev) (db-nth ns 0))
                      (set (extract d last) (reverse (cdr (reverse lasts))))
                      ;; `(`, then the shards.
                      (shards-scanned! d graph (i64+ at 1) n 0)
                      d)))))))))

"The keys the database has nodes of, in order of number."
(define-rec
  (im-keys (subr kfx (imap sexps) sexps)
    (lambda (t acc)
      (tagcase t
        (im-none () acc)
        (im-node (l k x h r) (im-keys l (cons (node-key x) (im-keys r acc))))))))

(define-rec
  (shards-read! (subr qe (db (listof i64 acyclic)) unit)
    (lambda (d ns) (if (null? ns) #u (begin (db-shard-read! d (car ns)) (shards-read! d (cdr ns)))))))

(define db-keys (subr qe (db) sexps)
  (lambda (d)
    (begin
      ;; Every shard read (C472): this one asks for all.
      (shards-read! d (sm-numbers (get (extract d shards)) nil))
      (im-keys (get (extract d nodes)) nil))))
